WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.968
A year long investigation is over.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.003
And John Durham,

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.038
the special counsel, investigating

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.640
whether there was any misconduct

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.641
by the FBI

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.176
in the Trump-Russia investigation

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.579
or just released his findings for years.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.747
As you may recall, Donald Trump

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:14.814
and his supporters

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.117
pinned their hopes on the investigation

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.184
by the former U.S.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.953
attorney for Connecticut, John Durham.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:20.987
Later named special counsel

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.322
by Attorney General Bill Barr.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.356
Trump and his allies

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.191
arguing that Durham would exonerate

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.527
him and his 2016 campaign and associates

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.896
from any hint of improper behavior.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.297
Regarding the Russian government's

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:32.732
attempts to interfere

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.701
in the 2016 election.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.302
Durham is coming

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.470
was the slogan

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.438
and the meme tweeted

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.306
by Republican lawmakers

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.741
and the president's

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.511
family hinting that Durham would lead to

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.812
bombshell indictments

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.881
of those who investigated Trump now.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.916
The bombshell indictments did not happen.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:50.884
Durham did

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:51.918
get one minor court

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.054
victory to court losses,

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:55.722
but President Trump appeared

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.690
so confident of what Durham would find,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.359
he openly pressured

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.126
the special counsel

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.061
to release his findings

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.096
before the 2020 election.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.798
Regardless, the report is now here.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.799
It has dropped,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.467
and it might not have produced everything

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.069
of what some Republicans hold for it.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.236
Is regardless.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.740
Devastating to the FBI and to a degree,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.775
it does exonerate Donald Trump.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:16.576
Let's bring in

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.311
CNN senior justice correspondent

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.079
Evan Perez.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.848
Evan, what exactly did Durham find

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:22.816
in this report?

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.418
Well, Jake, the

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:25.952
bottom line

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.720
finding from John Durham's

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.756
four year investigation

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.291
is that the FBI moved

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.026
very quickly to investigate

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:34.094
these allegations

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.995
of connections of collusion

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.231
between the Trump campaign and Russia

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:41.101
and that they did so by ignoring

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.602
a lot of evidence

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.137
that would have led them

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.472
to drop that altogether.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:46.739
He's saying that

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.609
they may have had reason to open

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.311
a preliminary investigation

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.045
and assessment.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:52.979
Perhaps these are very,

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.781
very low level investigations.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.649
But certainly what he finds is

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.518
that there wasn't enough there

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:01.921
to to to to support the FBI's decision

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.523
to open a full blown

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.125
investigation of this

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:08.461
of the Trump Russia ties back in 2016.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.462
I'll tell you

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.764
one part of what he writes here.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:12.665
He says

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.100
that it seems highly likely

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.002
that at a minimum confirmation

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.904
bias played a significant role

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.439
in the FBI's acceptance

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:22.442
of extraordinarily serious allegations

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:25.512
derived from uncorroborated information

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.213
that had not been subjected

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.081
to the typical

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.916
exacting analysis

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.951
that the FBI usually uses.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.188
He goes on to say that the FBI discounted

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:38.124
or willfully ignored material information

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.126
that did not support the narrative

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.095
of a collusive relationship

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.130
between Trump of Russia and Russia.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.633
There was a lot of very sharp criticism

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.902
here of the former FBI leadership,

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.070
James Comey and McCabe,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.438
who were running the FBI

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.707
and who oversaw a lot of these along,

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:55.875
a lot of the steps

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.912
that the the report goes into, Jake.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.014
But as you pointed out, bottom line,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.615
there are no additional charges.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.884
Nobody is bringing charges against Comey

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.486
or anybody else.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:07.220
That the former

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.588
President Trump

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.924
kept saying he expected them to.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.425
There was

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.694
a former Trump I'm sorry,

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.964
a former Clinton campaign outside lawyer

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.166
who was brought up on charges

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.301
he was acquitted.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.735
Again, in here, there's a

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.103
there's a footnote that points out

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.105
there is no chargeable crimes

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.308
against people in the Clinton campaign.

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:29.375
Again,

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.276
something that the

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.411
the former president

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.612
said he expected this

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.880
investigation to find, Jake.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:34.781
So it's very interesting.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.216
First of all, we should note

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.284
that when President Biden took office,

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.954
he there were 22 special counsels

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:41.788
or one U.S.

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.256
attorney, one special counsel

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.458
that he let continue doing their job.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.659
So one was John Durham

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:47.393
during this case,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.328
and the other one was the U.S.

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:49.262
attorney in Delaware

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.030
investigating Hunter.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.233
So that is why this was allowed to

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:54.000
proceed.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:55.802
A couple

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.803
quotes here from the

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.371
from Durham's report,

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.472
one based on the review

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.573
of CROSSFIRE hurricane,

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.175
that's the investigation into Trump

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:02.842
and Russia

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.410
and related intelligence activities.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.645
We conclude that the Justice Department

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.679
and FBI

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:10.083
failed to uphold their important mission

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.685
of strict fidelity to the law

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.953
in connection with certain events

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.989
and activities described in the report.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.257
And he says about,

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.291
quote, certain

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.293
about regarding certain personnel

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.996
intimately involved in the matter,

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:25.231
there was a, quote, predisposition

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:28.268
to open an investigation into Trump.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.471
He is basically saying he's these are not

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.939
criminal allegations,

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:33.906
but he is saying that

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.642
this was unprofessional.

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.677
And failed to meet the standards

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:40.113
of the Justice Department and the FBI.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:41.914
Jake,

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.150
the stunning thing about this report

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.653
is that we frankly know a lot of this.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.521
The the inspector

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.722
general of the Justice Department

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.392
did a 500 page report

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:55.161
that came out in late 2019

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.130
and that one

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.998
told us a lot of these findings

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.533
that Durham is now

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.535
is now confirming, frankly

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.170
one of the reasons why

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.472
Durham was brought on board

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.508
was supposedly to go beyond

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:09.509
what the inspector

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.311
general of the Justice Department

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.379
found in their investigation.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.681
And one of the things

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:15.348
it was supposed to do

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:17.083
was to tell us a lot about what

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.085
the intelligence community was doing.

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.186
It turns out

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:22.455
they didn't find very much there

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:24.090
in the intelligence community.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.425
And certainly not to support

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.026
the suspicions that they had,

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:30.330
that there was a cabal of of of people

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.097
from the FBI

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.498
and the intelligence community

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.567
who were out to get Donald Trump.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.703
That appears to have fallen flat

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:38.204
as part of this investigation.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.038
And so,

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.506
look, there's a lot in here

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:41.908
that should make

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.209
the FBI

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.577
have to come back and answer

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:45.411
some of the more questions,

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.013
including some of the changes

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:47.480
that they say

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.681
they've made to make sure

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.484
something like this never happens again.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:52.585
But the bottom line

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:53.519
from what

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.320
we see here

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.621
at the end of a four year

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.490
investigation really

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.559
doesn't tell us a hell of a lot more

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.461
than what we knew.

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:02.428
You know, a couple of years ago

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:03.129
when the inspector

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:03.663
general took

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:05.131
a look at many of these things

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:08.267
and came away with 17 troubled,

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.335
very big,

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.003
troubling findings

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:13.239
that they said the FBI needed to fix.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:13.740
Yeah.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.607
So another thing

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:17.777
so Rachel Cohen, who is a spokeswoman,

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.112
the communications, rather

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:21.280
communications director for Mark Warner,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.315
who is the chairman

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.049
of the Senate

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:25.017
Subcommittee on Intelligence,

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.552
she notes,

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.487
and this is an important

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:29.155
this is important context

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.723
that the Senate Intelligence Committee

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:31.157
spent three

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:31.758
and a half years

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.526
reviewing millions of documents

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.027
and interviewing hundreds of witnesses.

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:35.595
This is she writes

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.429
this on Twitter

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.063
and concluded

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.498
that the FBI had ample

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:42.301
cause for concern in 2006

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:43.503
And she notes that

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.404
that the committee,

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.538
the Senate Intelligence

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.506
Committee at the time

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.274
was led by Republicans.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:49.709
She's referring to former North

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:50.977
Carolina Senator

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.912
Richard Burr and again,

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:55.014
both of these facts can be true.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:55.948
At the same time,

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.049
it is possible

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.284
that the FBI

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:00.386
had legitimate cause for concern

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.522
and is also possible

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:05.057
that some individuals in the FBI

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:06.259
got ahead over their skis

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:07.560
and were not as professional

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.662
as they should have been. Right, exactly.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:10.263
And one of the things

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:11.798
you come away from here in this report,

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.232
and it was surprising to me to see him

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.300
say it

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.803
because because you remember

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.171
in 2019 Durham

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:19.972
came out with a

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:22.241
very highly unusual statement

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:22.608
in which

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.944
he said he disagreed

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:25.411
with a key

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.146
finding of the inspector general

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.147
which said that you know,

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.115
there was plenty of reason

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:31.017
for the Justice Department, for the FBI

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:32.852
to investigate the Trump campaign.

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.187
He said he disagreed with that.

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:37.356
In today's report, Durham says that

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.426
he sees reason for the FBI

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.961
to at least take a look

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:43.429
at some of the initial tips

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:45.031
that led to what became crossed

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:45.698
for a hurricane.

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:48.301
He's saying that the FBI had reason

00:07:48.568 --> 00:07:50.670
to investigate at least preliminary

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:51.771
What he doesn't see

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:52.805
is the reason

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:55.041
for a full blown investigation,

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.542
according to this report, Jake.

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:57.376
One of the interesting

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:59.479
one of the things that stood out to me,

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:01.080
if you remember the former president

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.648
kept saying that, you know, he

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.417
he was going to find evidence of

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.752
of of deep state spying.

00:08:06.953 --> 00:08:08.855
Well, there is a

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:09.355
part here

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:10.623
that talks about

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.725
a confidential human source,

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:14.126
essentially a spy

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:17.196
who was tasked with going to

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.532
a Clinton campaign fundraiser

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:21.400
Let me repeat that.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.836
A Clinton campaign fund raiser,

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.872
because the FBI had gotten

00:08:25.872 --> 00:08:26.572
some information

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.074
that somebody was saying that

00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:29.775
perhaps a foreign government

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.344
might be expecting some favors

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:33.346
from a future Clinton presidency.

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.047
So there you have it.

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:36.716
The FBI was spying

00:08:36.716 --> 00:08:38.117
on the Clinton campaign,

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:39.986
according to John Durham's report.

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:41.521
Has the FBI responded at all

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:43.155
to the Durham report?

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:45.191
They have the

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:48.060
the Christopher Wray, the FBI director,

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:48.995
put out a statement

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:49.829
just a little while ago

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:52.431
saying that a lot of the changes

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:54.800
that the FBI have has made

00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:56.102
will make sure

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:58.104
that things like this don't happen again.

00:08:58.104 --> 00:09:00.206
And you know, the FBI wants to point out,

00:09:00.473 --> 00:09:01.807
Jake, that,

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:03.175
you know, a lot of the leadership,

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:03.910
a lot of the people

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:06.045
who are involved in decisions

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:06.412
that are

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:07.113
that are in

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.447
for some very sharp criticism

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:09.282
in this report,

00:09:09.282 --> 00:09:11.551
they're gone from the FBI. Right.

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:12.218
And the current FBI

00:09:12.218 --> 00:09:13.686
director was appointed, as we as

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:14.854
we know,

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:16.155
by President Trump,

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:17.123
not that that has stopped him

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:18.291
from criticizing Christopher Wray.

00:09:18.291 --> 00:09:19.659
Evan Perez, thank you so much.

00:09:19.659 --> 00:09:21.027
Let's bring in former federal prosecutor

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:23.563
Ellie Honig and CNN's Sara Sara Murray.

00:09:23.596 --> 00:09:25.798
So here it is, all.

00:09:25.798 --> 00:09:27.033
300 plus pages.

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:29.101
Ali, the bottom line,

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:30.403
Durham has found that

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:31.504
the FBI, in his view,

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:32.872
should never have launched

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:35.174
a full blown investigation

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:37.243
into relationships

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:38.611
or allegations of relationships

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:39.812
between Trump

00:09:39.812 --> 00:09:41.180
and his associates in his campaign

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.515
and the Russian government.

00:09:42.515 --> 00:09:43.482
What's your response?

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:43.983
Well, Jake, there's

00:09:43.983 --> 00:09:45.585
no surprise in that conclusion.

00:09:45.585 --> 00:09:46.252
It was really sort

00:09:46.252 --> 00:09:47.853
of a foregone conclusion from the start.

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:48.821
Let's remember

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.156
how John Durham came

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:51.691
to be special counsel

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:53.025
in the middle of 2019.

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:54.160
When Mueller concluded

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.461
his investigation, Donald Trump

00:09:55.461 --> 00:09:57.363
was taking to Twitter regularly

00:09:57.363 --> 00:09:59.632
saying all caps investigate

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:00.533
the investigators.

00:10:00.533 --> 00:10:01.067
And shortly

00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:03.069
thereafter, Bill Barr appointed

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:04.837
John Durham to do this investigation.

00:10:04.837 --> 00:10:06.105
And there was a really important

00:10:06.105 --> 00:10:07.773
and I think, revealing moment

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:09.842
in December of 2019

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:11.344
DOJ's own inspector

00:10:11.344 --> 00:10:13.412
general came out with a finding that yes,

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:15.214
the FBI made several missteps

00:10:15.214 --> 00:10:16.248
and Durham seizes

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:17.450
on some of these as well.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.552
However, there was ample ground

00:10:19.552 --> 00:10:20.853
to open an investigation.

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:22.054
And right away

00:10:22.054 --> 00:10:23.089
John Durham came out

00:10:23.089 --> 00:10:23.956
with a public statement

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:25.358
and said I disagree with that.

00:10:25.358 --> 00:10:27.393
That was three and change years

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:27.994
ago, Jake.

00:10:27.994 --> 00:10:29.729
So it doesn't mean Durham's

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:31.230
findings are valid or invalid,

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.798
but there's absolutely no surprise

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:33.933
that he's come out where he has.

